{"unit":6,"section":1,"cefr":"Intro","objective":"form basic sentences","skill":"There is/To Have","heading":"Form basic sentences","phrases":[{"he":"יש חלב?","en":"Is there any milk?","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/f8a9f2cee57c5b2875af785c308f4d12","tokens":[{"w":"יש","h":["there is","there are","have"]},{"w":"חלב","h":["milk"]}]},{"he":"אין מים!","en":"There is no water!","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/32a9f9c35516ce6df69b744f39dea52d","tokens":[{"w":"אין","h":["there is no","not have","not has"]},{"w":"מים","h":["water"]}]},{"he":"יש לי תפוח.","en":"I have an apple.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/afd5502b24e09d1d87c2454fe791eec4","tokens":[{"w":"יש","h":["I have","have","there are","has"]},{"w":"לי","h":["I have","me","to me","for me"]},{"w":"תפוח","h":["an apple","apple"]}]},{"he":"אין להם כלב.","en":"They don't have a dog.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/8224cc66bc65b41395645cfd8f8c9b7e","tokens":[{"w":"אין","h":["they do not have","not have","there is no","not has"]},{"w":"להם","h":["they do not have","to them","them"]},{"w":"כלב","h":["a dog","dog"]}]}],"sentences":[{"he":"יש חלב?","en":"Is there milk?","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/f8a9f2cee57c5b2875af785c308f4d12"},{"he":"יש יין!","en":"There is wine!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין יין.","en":"There is no wine.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"אין להן.","en":"They do not have.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין מים!","en":"There is no water!","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/32a9f9c35516ce6df69b744f39dea52d"},{"he":"יש אהבה!","en":"There is love!","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"אין אורז?","en":"There is no rice?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לזה דרך?","en":"Does it have a way?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לי תפוח.","en":"I have an apple.","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/afd5502b24e09d1d87c2454fe791eec4"},{"he":"יש לךָ ספר.","en":"You have a book.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לךָ ספר?","en":"Do you have a book?","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"יש לכן כלב.","en":"You have a dog.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לנו עוף.","en":"We have chicken.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לה חמאה.","en":"She has butter.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"אין לה תפוז.","en":"She does not have an orange.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין להם כלב.","en":"They don't have a dog.","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/8224cc66bc65b41395645cfd8f8c9b7e"},{"he":"אין לו תפוח.","en":"He does not have an apple.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין לי תפוח.","en":"I do not have an apple.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין לכם חלב?","en":"Don't you have milk?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לה אפרסק.","en":"She has a peach.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"יש לךְ אהבה!","en":"You have love!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין לו מרתף.","en":"It does not have a basement.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"הם עונים לי.","en":"They are answering me.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"אין לה ילדים.","en":"She doesn't have children.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין לי עיתון.","en":"I don't have a newspaper.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין לכן עוגה?","en":"Don't you have a cake?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לךְ ילדים?","en":"Do you have children?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לנו ילדים.","en":"We have children.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש תפוח ולחם.","en":"There is an apple and bread.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"לילד יש תפוח.","en":"The boy has an apple.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אני שולח לךָ.","en":"I am sending to you.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"זה מתאים לךָ!","en":"It fits you!","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"אין לךָ משאית?","en":"Don't you have a truck?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש להם כלב רע.","en":"They have a bad dog.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"לגברים יש חלב!","en":"The men have milk!","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"הוא הופך לילד.","en":"He is becoming a child.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"הם קוראים לנו!","en":"They are calling us!","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"יש לו חלב ולחם.","en":"He has milk and bread.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לכם כלב טוב.","en":"You have a good dog.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"לךְ יש חלב, לא?","en":"You have milk, don't you?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין להם עניבות.","en":"They do not have ties.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"לחיות יש שאלות.","en":"The animals have questions.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"אבא, יש לו אורז!","en":"Dad, he has rice!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין להם יין טוב.","en":"They don't have good wine.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לזה חלב טעים.","en":"It has tasty milk.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לנו מיץ טעים!","en":"We have tasty juice!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"לכן יש, לנו אין!","en":"You have, we do not!","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"אין לחם ואין יין.","en":"There is no bread and there is no wine.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"האם ליונה יש מים?","en":"Does the dove have water?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לזה אגוז יפֶה.","en":"It has a pretty nut.","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"אתם לא עוזרים לי.","en":"You do not help me.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"סליחה, יש לכם ספר?","en":"Excuse me, do you have a book?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"יש לי גלידה במקרר.","en":"I have ice cream in the refrigerator.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"יש זבובים מעל הפרות.","en":"There are flies above the cows.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"האם יש להן תפוח חמוץ?","en":"Do they have a sour apple?","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אין בעד מה, לילה טוב.","en":"You are welcome, good night.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"יש לנו חדר אוכל גדול.","en":"We have a big dining room.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"סביר להניח שאין לו ילדים.","en":"Presumably he does not have children.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1}],"hints":{"יש":"I have / do you have / has","חלב":"milk","יין":"wine","אין":"not has / not have / nothing can be done","להן":"to them / they (f)","מים":"water","אהבה":"love","אורז":"rice","דרך":"path / road / way","לי":"I have / for me / me","תפוח":"an apple / apple","לךָ":"to you / you / do you have","ספר":"a book / book / tell! (Story)","לכן":"that's why / therefore / you","כלב":"a dog / dog","לנו":"for us / to us / us","עוף":"a chicken / chicken, fowl, poultry (Food)","לה":"her / it (feminine nouns) / she has","חמאה":"butter","תפוז":"an orange / orange / orange (Fruit)","להם":"them / they do not have / to them","לו":"if / if (cond.) / to him","לכם":"do you have / to you (pl. masc.) / you","אפרסק":"a peach / peach","לךְ":"to you / you / do you have","מרתף":"basement, cellar","הם":"are / they / they are","עונים":"m.p. / m.p - pres.","ילדים":"boys / children / kids","עיתון":"a newspaper / newspaper","עוגה":"a cake / cake","אני":"I / I am / I am a girl","שולח":"m.s.","זה":"it / it is / it's","מתאים":"fits, matches, is compatible","משאית":"truck","רע":"bad / bad (m.s)","הוא":"(he) is / (it) is / he","הופך":"m.s.","קוראים":"read (m.p - pres.) / m.p.","טוב":"alright / good / ok","לא":"aren't / didn't / do not","עניבות":"tie","שאלות":"question, query / matter (Colloq.)","אבא":"dad / father / father, dad","טעים":"delicious / tasty / tasty (m.s)","מיץ":"a glass of juice / juice","לחם":"bread","האם":"do / does / is","אגוז":"nut","יפֶה":"beautiful / beautiful (sg. fem.) / handsome","אתם":"do you want / you / you are","עוזרים":"m.p.","סליחה":"I am sorry / pardon / excuse me","גלידה":"ice cream","זבובים":"fly","מעל":"above (Prep)","חמוץ":"sour / sour (m.s)","מה":"everything / nothing can be done / there is nothing to do","לילה":"night","חדר":"room","אוכל":"eat / eating / eats","גדול":"big"},"words":[{"he":"יש","en":"have","alt":["I have","do you have","has","she has","there are","there is","we have"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"yesh"},{"he":"לי","en":"me","alt":["I have","for me","to me"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"li"},{"he":"אין","en":"not has","alt":["not have","nothing can be done","there is no","there is nothing to do","they do not have"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"ein"},{"he":"כלב","en":"dog","alt":["a dog"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"kelev"},{"he":"חלב","en":"milk","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"khalav"},{"he":"להם","en":"them","alt":["they do not have","to them"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"lahem"},{"he":"לכם","en":"you","alt":["do you have","to you (pl. masc.)","you have (p.m.)"],"from":"skill","tr":"lakhem"},{"he":"לךָ","en":"to you","alt":["you"],"from":"skill","tr":"l'kha"},{"he":"לנו","en":"us","alt":["for us","to us","we have","we will not have"],"from":"skill","tr":"lanu"},{"he":"לה","en":"her","alt":["it (feminine nouns)","she has","to her"],"from":"skill","tr":"lah"},{"he":"לו","en":"To Him","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"lo"},{"he":"להן","en":"To Them","alt":["They (f)"],"from":"skill","tr":"lahen"},{"he":"לכן","en":"That's why","alt":["you","therefore"],"from":"skill","tr":"lakhen"},{"he":"מים","en":"water","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"mayim"},{"he":"תפוח","en":"apple","alt":["an apple"],"from":"phrase","tr":"tapuakh"}],"lexemes":["לכם","לךָ","להם","לי","לנו","לה","לךְ","לו","להן","לכן","לזה","לילד","לגברים","ליונה","אין","ואין"],"tips":"To Have\n-----------\nIn Hebrew, there is no verb \"to have\". Instead, in the present tense, we use the word \"יש\"(yesh) - \"there is\" and a conjugation of the preposition \"ל\" (le = \"to\").\n\nFor example, \"לנו\" (lanu) = to us. Using it together with \"יש\" (yesh = there is) will form: \n\nיש לנו (yesh lanu) = we have (literally, \"there is to us\").\n\nHere is a table of indirect pronouns with יש:\n\nEnglish | Hebrew | Pronunciation\n---|---|---\nI have | יש לי | yesh li\nYou have (s.m) | ָיש לך | yesh lechá\nYou have (s.f.) | ְיש לך | yesh lach\nHe has | יש לו | yesh lo\nShe has | יש לה | yesh la\nWe have | יש לנו | yesh lánu\nYou have (p.m.) | יש לכם | yesh lakhém\nYou have (p.f.) | יש לכן | yesh lakhén\nThey have (m.) | יש להם | yesh lahém\nThey have (f.) | יש להן | yesh lahén\n\nWhen using \"you (plural) have\" or \"they have\" for a mixed group, use the masculine plural.\n\nIf we want to say that one does not have something, we use the word \"אין\" (\"ein\", but mostly pronounced colloquially as \"en\") instead of \"יש\".\n\nFor example:\n\n* **יש** לי תפוח - I have an apple\n\n* **אין** לי תפוח - I don't have an apple  (literally \"there is not to me apple\")\n\nSimilarly, we add \"ל\" (le = \"to\") to any other noun that is the possessor of something:\n\nFor example: \n\nל + ילד = לילד = **le**yéled - to a boy\nיש לילד - a boy has\n\nIf we are adding ל to an object that has ה (the) already attached at the beginning, we remove ה and add ל. The pronunciation will be \"la\", not \"le\":\n\nל + הילד = לילד = **la**yéled - to *the* boy\n\nHow do we know whether לילד means \"to a boy\" or \"to the boy\"? Context! (Or if there is nikud: לְילד versus לַילד).\n\n----------\nWord Order\n-----------\n\nUsually the word order for sentences referring to possession is as follows (reading right to left):\n\nthing possessed + possessor + יש + ל \n\nFor example:  \nיש לילד תפוח  \nאין לילד תפוח\n\nAn alternative order places the possessor at the start of the sentence, as follows:  \nלילד יש תפוח  \nThis has the effect of placing more emphasis on the possessor than on the object possessed: \"the **boy** (it's the boy, and not the girl, or the frog) has an apple\". \n \nThis example may help you to understand the difference:  \nלילד יש תפוח, אבל לי אין  \n***the boy*** has an apple, but ***I*** don't."}